# Site origin configuration (SEO)
#
# Copy this file to site-origin.txt (gitignored) OR set the SITE_ORIGIN
# environment variable in the Netlify build settings.
#
# Planned production canonical host (when DNS / ownership / SSL are ready):
#   https://signalcrestsystems.com
#
# Validation rules (enforced by scripts/build-public.mjs):
# - https only (non-HTTPS schemes rejected)
# - No trailing slash
# - Scheme + host only — no path, query, or fragment
# - No username or password (userinfo rejected)
# - No explicit port (including :443)
# - No localhost or *.localhost
# - No bare IPv4 or IPv6 addresses
# - No placeholder example.com / example.org / example.net (or www variants)
# - Prefer the apex host (signalcrestsystems.com) as the canonical origin
# - Do not commit a fabricated or unverified production domain into the repo
# - Do not hardcode a production hostname into public HTML templates
#
# Local / origin-optional builds (default):
# - When unset, the build still succeeds:
#     * robots.txt is emitted without a Sitemap line
#     * sitemap.xml is omitted from dist/
#     * absolute canonical / og:url / og:image / twitter:image tags are omitted
#       from generated HTML (no relative or placeholder SEO URLs)
# - When set to a validated origin, the build injects absolute SEO URLs for the
#   10 public pages and writes sitemap.xml + a robots Sitemap directive
#
# Production-release mode (origin REQUIRED — fail closed):
# - Independent of NODE_ENV. Do not rely on NODE_ENV=production for this gate.
# - Enable with either:
#     SCS_PRODUCTION_RELEASE=1   (or true)
#     — or —
#     node scripts/build-public.mjs --production-release
# - When enabled without SITE_ORIGIN / site-origin.txt, the build FAILS.
#
# Local rebuild (origin optional):
#   node scripts/build-public.mjs
#
# Local test with approved origin:
#   set SITE_ORIGIN=https://signalcrestsystems.com
#   node scripts/build-public.mjs
#
# Production-release invocation (PowerShell example):
#   $env:SCS_PRODUCTION_RELEASE = "1"
#   $env:SITE_ORIGIN = "https://signalcrestsystems.com"
#   node scripts/build-public.mjs
#
# Production-release via CLI flag (origin still required via env or site-origin.txt):
#   $env:SITE_ORIGIN = "https://signalcrestsystems.com"
#   node scripts/build-public.mjs --production-release
#
# Netlify (when activating production publish): set both environment variables
# in the site build settings:
#   SCS_PRODUCTION_RELEASE = 1
#   SITE_ORIGIN = https://signalcrestsystems.com
# Keep the build command as: node scripts/build-public.mjs
#
# Intended redirect (NOT activated yet):
#   Permanently redirect https://www.signalcrestsystems.com → https://signalcrestsystems.com
#   Do not add Netlify _redirects / domain aliases for this until DNS ownership
#   and both hostnames are verified. This file documents intent only.
#   DNS / SSL verification is not claimed here.
